    {
      "id": "secrets-store-and-access",
      "question": "Where does Aurora Commerce store its application secrets, and how do workloads read them?",
      "answer": "Aurora Commerce stores application secrets in Azure Key Vault, specifically the production vault `kv-aurora-prod`\u30105:0\u2020source\u3011\u30105:3\u2020source\u3011.\n\nWorkloads read secrets at runtime using managed identity; the standard pattern is either the Key Vault provider for the Secrets Store CSI driver or the Azure Identity SDK, both using the pod\u2019s managed identity\u30105:0\u2020source\u3011\u30105:1\u2020source\u3011. Access is least-privilege: each AKS workload gets `get` only on the secrets it needs, scoped to `kv-aurora-prod`\u30105:0\u2020source\u3011.\n\nA few related guardrails are explicit:\n- No static Key Vault credentials, service principal passwords, or connection strings are mounted into pods\u30105:0\u2020source\u3011.\n- Secrets are not committed to code, baked into images, or set as literal Kubernetes values\u30105:1\u2020source\u3011.\n- Key Vault reads are audited\u30105:1\u2020source\u3011.",
      "citations": [
